## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design extensible components with runtime pluggability, using the Strategy and Registry patterns in a beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern
- Registry pattern for runtime extensibility
- TTL-aware caching and eviction semantics
- Thread-safety considerations in JS/TS environments

## Code Example

```javascript
interface EvictionPolicy<K,V> {
  evict(store: Map<K,V>): K;
  onAccess?(key: K, value: V): void;
  onInsert?(key: K, value: V): void;
}
class RuntimePolicyRegistry<K,V> {
  private policies = new Map<string, ()=>EvictionPolicy<K,V>>();
  register(name: string, factory: ()=>EvictionPolicy<K,V>): void { this.policies.set(name, factory); }
